pathogenesis.

107
00:05:46,950 --> 00:05:49,570
In brief, after
bronchial obstruction,

108
00:05:49,730 --> 00:05:51,430
the blood
circulating in the

109
00:05:51,430 --> 00:05:53,250
alveolar capillary
membrane will

110
00:05:53,250 --> 00:05:55,270
absorb the gas
from the alveoli.

111
00:05:55,410 --> 00:05:57,550
This gas absorption will

112
00:05:57,550 --> 00:05:59,230
induce retraction
of the lung.

113
00:05:59,730 --> 00:06:02,370
Subsequently, in
few hours, the

114
00:06:02,370 --> 00:06:04,690
affected alveoli
will be airless.

115
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:07,090
However, the
blood flow will

116
00:06:07,090 --> 00:06:09,350
reach an airless
unventilated lung

117
00:06:09,350 --> 00:06:12,490
and arterial
hypoxemia ensues.

118
00:06:12,910 --> 00:06:15,330
The blood leaving
the lung will

119
00:06:15,330 --> 00:06:17,810
not be oxygenated.
Meantime,

120
00:06:18,030 --> 00:06:19,830
secretions and
dead cells will

121
00:06:19,830 --> 00:06:22,190
accumulate in the
alveoli, preventing

122
00:06:22,190 --> 00:06:24,450
the collapse
of this lung.

123
00:06:26,210 --> 00:06:27,290
However,

124
00:06:27,690 --> 00:06:29,650
the surrounding
healthy lung will

125
00:06:29,650 --> 00:06:32,370
distend and there
is a mediastinal

126
00:06:32,370 --> 00:06:34,270
shift towards the
affected lung.

127
00:06:34,830 --> 00:06:36,290
In addition,

128
00:06:36,750 --> 00:06:38,910
the diaphragm will
be elevated while

129
00:06:38,910 --> 00:06:41,050
the chest wall
will become flat.

130
00:06:41,770 --> 00:06:44,670
On the right side
of this slide there

131
00:06:44,670 --> 00:06:46,050
