134
00:06:58,950 --> 00:07:00,310
Compression athelectasis.

135
00:07:00,730 --> 00:07:03,870
As mentioned previously
compression athelectasis

136
00:07:03,870 --> 00:07:05,950
is determined by
a pleural effusion

137
00:07:05,950 --> 00:07:08,950
associated with cardiac
failure or cancer.

138
00:07:09,110 --> 00:07:11,910
It is also determined
by accumulation of

139
00:07:11,910 --> 00:07:15,110
blood or air in the
pleural cavity, more

140
00:07:15,110 --> 00:07:17,910
specifically hemothorax
or pneumothorax.

141
00:07:18,120 --> 00:07:20,930
It is also seen in
conditions in which there

142
00:07:20,930 --> 00:07:24,290
is an elevated diaphragm
such as in bedridden

143
00:07:24,290 --> 00:07:27,250
patients, after
surgery, and in ositis.

144
00:07:27,810 --> 00:07:31,030
The drawing included in
this slide summarizes

145
00:07:31,030 --> 00:07:33,070
the pathogenesis
of this condition,

146
00:07:33,090 --> 00:07:35,650
specifically accumulation
of the fluid,

147
00:07:35,650 --> 00:07:37,690
blood, or air within
pleural cavity.

148
00:07:38,390 --> 00:07:40,150
Please note that
in compression

149
00:07:40,150 --> 00:07:43,250
aphelactasis, the
mediastinum and trachea are

150
00:07:43,250 --> 00:07:45,830
pushed away towards
the healthy lung.

151
00:07:46,210 --> 00:07:49,610
On X-ray, there is an
increased transparency

152
00:07:49,610 --> 00:07:52,730
of the lung field
and a hyper-resonance

153
00:07:52,730 --> 00:07:55,030
is recorded on
physical examination.

154
00:07:56,810 --> 00:08:00,310
Contraction aphylectasis
This is also known

155
00:08:00,310 --> 00:08:02,670
as cicatrization
aphylectasis and is

156
00:08:02,670 --> 00:08:06,130
determined by a reduction
of lung volumes following

157
00:08:06,130 --> 00:08:08,430
extensive severe
parenchyma scarring.

158
00:08:09,300 --> 00:08:11,910
This type of defective
healing is seen in

159
00:08:11,910 --> 00:08:14,270
lung tuberculosis,
which is a granulomatous

160
00:08:14,270 --> 00:08:16,290
inflammation of the
lung parenchyma.

161
00:08:17,630 --> 00:08:20,010
Severe parenchyma
scarring is also

162
00:08:20,010 --> 00:08:21,890
seen in necrotizing
pneumonia.

163
00:08:23,550 --> 00:08:26,210
Anyway, the most
important morphological

164
00:08:26,210 --> 00:08:28,030
anomaly seen in
this patient,

165
00:08:28,030 --> 00:08:30,290
apart from lung
parenchyma scarring,

166
00:08:30,570 --> 00:08:33,170
is bronchial
scarring, leading to

167
00:08:33,170 --> 00:08:36,190
significant narrowing
of the bronchial lumen.

168
00:08:37,090 --> 00:08:39,510
The image included
in this slide

169
00:08:39,510 --> 00:08:41,710
shows the left
and right lungs

170
00:08:41,710 --> 00:08:44,510
removed during an
autopsy of a patient

171
00:08:44,510 --> 00:08:46,790
with contraction
athelectasis.

172
00:08:47,770 --> 00:08:50,430
As you might see,
the left lung and

173
00:08:50,430 --> 00:08:52,810
the middle and the
lower lobes of the

174
00:08:52,810 --> 00:08:55,170
right lung are
totally collapsed,

175
00:08:55,170 --> 00:08:58,110
while the upper lobe
of the right lung

176
00:08:58,150 --> 00:08:59,910
seem to be inflated.

177
00:09:10,850 --> 00:09:12,830
Now I would like to
discuss a special

178
00:09:12,830 --> 00:09:15,370
form of athelectasis,
the respiratory

179
00:09:15,370 --> 00:09:18,290
distress syndrome
in newborns, RDS,

180
00:09:18,850 --> 00:09:22,010
also known as neonatal
respiratory distress

181
00:09:22,010 --> 00:09:26,050
syndrome or hyaline
membrane disease.

182
00:09:29,070 --> 00:09:31,350
What's happening
in this setting?

183
00:09:31,970 --> 00:09:35,250
Well at birth the
lungs inflate with air

184
00:09:35,250 --> 00:09:39,770
and the airways remain
open due to surfactant.

185
00:09:39,870 --> 00:09:43,010
Surfactant is a
mixture of lipids,

186
00:09:43,010 --> 00:09:45,970
proteins, glycoproteins,
lecithin and

187
00:09:45,970 --> 00:09:49,250
sphingomyelin secreted
by pneumocytes type 2.

188
00:09:49,990 --> 00:09:53,270
This factor maintains
the stability of

189
00:09:53,270 --> 00:09:55,450
pulmonary tissue by
reducing the surface

190
00:09:55,450 --> 00:09:57,790
tension in the small
-caliber airways.

191
00:09:58,250 --> 00:10:01,230
This decreased surface
tension prevents the

192
00:10:01,230 --> 00:10:03,850
collapse of these
airways on expiration.

193
00:10:04,870 --> 00:10:08,810
Regarding the production
of surfactant, it

194
00:10:08,810 --> 00:10:12,370
begins around 28
weeks in utero and it

195
00:10:12,370 --> 00:10:15,490
reaches its peak
around the 35th week of

196
00:10:15,490 --> 00:10:20,850
pregnancy and is modulated
by glucocorticoids.

197
00:10:22,950 --> 00:10:25,590
Therefore, if a
delivery takes place

198
00:10:25,590 --> 00:10:28,190
before the term,
the newborns must be

199
00:10:28,190 --> 00:10:31,150
treated with
glucocorticoids, which

200
00:10:31,150 --> 00:10:32,910
would increase
the synthesis of

201
00:10:32,910 --> 00:10:36,950
surfactant and newborn
********* babies.

202
00:10:37,910 --> 00:10:40,890
RDS is seen not
only in prematurity,

203
00:10:40,890 --> 00:10:42,310
but also in babies from

204
00:10:42,310 --> 00:10:44,230
mothers with
diabetes mellitus.

205
00:10:44,870 --> 00:10:49,170
Anyway, the newborns
with RDS will present

206
00:10:49,170 --> 00:10:51,810
with harsh respiratory
noises or grunting,

207
00:10:52,270 --> 00:10:54,250
tachymnea or
fast breathing,

208
00:10:54,830 --> 00:10:57,390
intercostal
retraction, and an

209
00:10:57,390 --> 00:10:59,570
abnormal lecithin
to sphingomyelin

210
00:10:59,570 --> 00:11:01,650
ratio of less than 1.5.

211
00:11:02,360 --> 00:11:05,950
Despite modern therapies,
RDS is the most

212
00:11:05,950 --> 00:11:08,570
common single cause
of death in the first

213
00:11:08,570 --> 00:11:11,570
month of life in the
Western countries.

214
00:11:13,110 --> 00:11:16,090
RDS is associated
with blindness,

215
00:11:16,730 --> 00:11:18,810
bronchopulmonary
dysplasia,

216
00:11:19,830 --> 00:11:22,110
cardiac anomalies such as

217
00:11:22,110 --> 00:11:24,150
patent ductus arteriosus,

218
00:11:25,230 --> 00:11:27,150
intraventricular
hemorrhage,

219
00:11:27,150 --> 00:11:28,530
and hypoglycemia.

220
00:11:29,550 --> 00:11:32,650
The characteristic
histopathology seen

221
00:11:32,650 --> 00:11:37,290
in newborns who died
from RDS represented

222
00:11:37,290 --> 00:11:39,670
the basis for the
old label of this

223
00:11:39,670 --> 00:11:42,470
condition as hyaline
membrane disease.

224
00:11:44,230 --> 00:11:47,350
The right side
microphotographs shows

225
00:11:47,350 --> 00:11:50,030
a hematoxylineosin
stained tissue

226
00:11:50,030 --> 00:11:52,790
section taken from
a baby with RDS.

227
00:11:53,370 --> 00:11:57,030
The lung is congested,
showing numerous

228
00:11:57,030 --> 00:12:00,410
dilated capillaries,
but more importantly

229
00:12:00,410 --> 00:12:03,430
the alveoli are lined
by hyaline membranes

230
00:12:03,430 --> 00:12:06,790
which appear as
eosinophilic pink and are

231
00:12:06,790 --> 00:12:09,730
made of fibrin and
epithelial dead cells.

232
00:12:11,320 --> 00:12:13,520
Overall, the lung
is collapsed.

233
00:12:14,110 --> 00:12:16,750
As a result of
deposition of hyaline

234
00:12:16,750 --> 00:12:20,150
membranes, blood which
passes through lungs, is

235
00:12:20,150 --> 00:12:24,040
unable to pick up
oxygen and unload CO2.

236
00:12:25,190 --> 00:12:30,210
Blood oxygen level
falls and CO2 increases,

237
00:12:30,210 --> 00:12:33,190
resulting in
acidosis and hypoxia.

238
00:12:35,930 --> 00:12:38,590
Promoedema represents
the accumulation of

239
00:12:38,590 --> 00:12:42,070
excessive interstitial
fluid in the alveoli.

240
00:12:43,170 --> 00:12:45,910
This large amount of
fluid accumulation

241
00:12:45,910 --> 00:12:48,770
results either as a
result of hemodynamic

242
00:12:48,770 --> 00:12:52,430
abnormalities or after
microvascular injury.

243
00:12:53,260 --> 00:12:54,590
Therefore, we have two

244
00:12:54,590 --> 00:12:56,110
major types of edema,

245
00:12:56,790 --> 00:13:00,370
hemodynamic
edema and edema

246
00:13:00,370 --> 00:13:02,870
associated with
microvascular injury.

247
00:13:04,550 --> 00:13:07,530
Hemodynamic edema is
seen in congestive

248
00:13:07,530 --> 00:13:11,110
heart failure and other
conditions associated

249
00:13:11,110 --> 00:13:13,410
with an increased
left heart pressure

250
00:13:13,410 --> 00:13:17,830
and impaired heart
contractility, such

251
00:13:17,830 --> 00:13:20,630
as coronary artery
disease, hypertension,

252
00:13:21,230 --> 00:13:23,010
valvular disease,
and dilated

253
00:13:23,010 --> 00:13:26,550
cardiomyopathy, various
metabolic conditions

254
00:13:26,550 --> 00:13:29,870
such as hypothyroidism,
myocarditis,

255
00:13:30,390 --> 00:13:31,870
ventricular hypertrophy

256
00:13:31,870 --> 00:13:33,510
and outflow obstruction.

257
