syndrome of newborn,

554
00:29:43,520 --> 00:29:46,210
including the role
of surfactant in

555
00:29:46,210 --> 00:29:48,410
the etiopathogenesis
of this condition.

556
00:29:49,480 --> 00:29:52,170
Then we have presented
the major forms

557
00:29:52,170 --> 00:29:54,350
of pulmonary edema,
the hemodynamic

558
00:29:54,350 --> 00:29:56,970
pulmonary edema, and
the microvascular

559
00:29:56,970 --> 00:29:59,230
injury-associated
pulmonary edema.

560
00:29:59,950 --> 00:30:02,790
Hemodynamic pulmonary
edema is seen in

561
00:30:02,790 --> 00:30:05,970
congestive heart
failure or in conditions

562
00:30:05,970 --> 00:30:08,490
associated with increased
left heart pressure.

563
00:30:08,850 --> 00:30:11,350
In both these
settings the

564
00:30:11,350 --> 00:30:13,210
hydrostatic pressure
is increased.

565
00:30:14,070 --> 00:30:16,590
There is decreased
cardiac output

566
00:30:16,590 --> 00:30:18,230
and the renin-angiotensin

567
00:30:18,230 --> 00:30:20,250
-aldosterone pathway
is activated

568
00:30:20,590 --> 00:30:22,930
with retention of
sodium and water

569
00:30:22,930 --> 00:30:25,470
which increases
venous pressure

570
00:30:25,470 --> 00:30:27,510
and results in
edema formation.

571
00:30:30,330 --> 00:30:33,290
Hemodynamic pulmonary
edema is also

572
00:30:33,290 --> 00:30:37,190
seen in patients
with low levels of

573
00:30:37,190 --> 00:30:41,510
albumin with loss of
oncotic pressure, as

574
00:30:41,510 --> 00:30:44,090
noted in liver
failure, protein-losing

575
00:30:44,090 --> 00:30:46,370
enteropathy, and
nephrotic syndrome.

576
00:30:48,030 --> 00:30:50,550
We have also discussed
the mycovascular

577
00:30:50,550 --> 00:30:52,770
injury-associated
pulmonary edema,

578
00:30:53,270 --> 00:30:55,370
which is determined
by injury to

579
00:30:55,370 --> 00:30:57,490
the alveolar
capillary endothelium.

580
00:30:57,550 --> 00:31:01,390
We have explained
the etiology and at

581
00:31:01,390 --> 00:31:05,430
the end of the session
we have debated the

582
00:31:05,430 --> 00:31:08,590
ARDS, acute respiratory
distress syndrome,

583
00:31:08,590 --> 00:31:11,050
which is a diagnosis
of exclusion.

584
00:31:11,930 --> 00:31:14,470
ARDS results after
a significant

585
00:31:14,470 --> 00:31:17,580
damage of alveolar
epithelium.

586
00:31:18,490 --> 00:31:21,970
It has three distinct
physiopathological

587
00:31:21,970 --> 00:31:25,210
phases, an exudative
phase followed by

588
00:31:25,210 --> 00:31:27,910
a proliferative and
a fibrotic phase,

589
00:31:27,910 --> 00:31:30,650
and is characterized
by abnormal chest

590
00:31:30,650 --> 00:31:34,330
X-ray, respiratory
failure, a decreased

591
00:31:34,330 --> 00:31:37,190
ratio of partial
pressure of oxygen to

592
00:31:37,190 --> 00:31:40,330
a fraction of
inspired oxygen, and

593
00:31:40,330 --> 00:31:43,050
symptoms of respiratory
failure in the absence

594
00:31:43,050 --> 00:31:45,730
of heart failure
or fluid overload.

